From e16c4185ce6e8c9edc71c5b0bb77571dca5e78ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwen35 <qwen35@local>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:09:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] [GPU] Fuse the Gated-DeltaNet SiLUs into their producers

Qwen3.5's linear-attention block applies SiLU in two places and both end up as a
standalone activation kernel that re-reads and re-writes the whole tensor:

  PagedCausalConv1D -> Reshape -> Swish   ([tokens, 6144], ~13 ms / 1k-token prefill)
  in_proj_z FC      -> Reshape -> Swish   ([tokens, 2048],  ~4 ms)

prepare_primitive_fusing only looks at a node's direct dependency, and the Reshape
that PagedCausalConv1DFusion/FC leave in between blocks the fusion. ov::pass::
MoveEltwiseUpThroughDataMov does not match ov::op::v4::Swish (it derives from Op).

* New pass MoveSwishUpThroughReshape: Swish(Reshape(x)) -> Reshape(Swish(x)) for a
  single-consumer Reshape (value-identical).
* prepare_primitive_fusing: allow a swish activation to fuse into paged_causal_conv1d.
* paged_causal_conv1d_ref: SWISH epilogue with the rounding order of the stand-alone
  activation kernel (round to f16 first, then SiLU in f16). The stand-alone kernel
  evaluates exp() on a half4, the epilogue on a scalar half, so the last f16 bit can
  differ: the first token was identical in the original study, a long greedy decode is
  not guaranteed to be.
* The in_proj_z Swish becomes the existing oneDNN eltwise_swish FC post-op. This one is
  evaluated on the f32 accumulator (more accurate, not bit-identical).

Switches: OV_DISABLE_SWISH_HOIST=1 turns the pass off; OV_SWISH_HOIST_PRODUCER_ONLY=1
hoists only over PagedCausalConv1D and leaves the in_proj_z SiLU as a separate kernel.
CMake: the plugin glob gets CONFIGURE_DEPENDS so an existing build tree picks up the
new source file.
